    "chapter_name": "Motion In One Dimension",
    "year": "2022",
    "shift": "shift_2"
  },
  "question": {
    "text": "An object of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> is thrown vertically upwards from the ground. The air resistance produces a constant retarding force of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> throughout the motion. The ratio of time of ascent to the time of descent will be equal to : [Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>:</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>3</mn></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Net force while going upward will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Similarly,&nbsp;Net force while going downward&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>40</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>t</mi><mrow><mi>u</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>t</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>"
  }
}